  "question": {
    "text": "<p>Which reactant will give the following alcohol on reaction with one mole of phenyl magnesium bromide&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mi>PhMgBr</mi></mfenced></math>&nbsp;followed by acidic hydrolysis?</p><p><img src=\"assets\\qt0060_0eabda92f194.png\" style=\"width: 118px; height: 120px;\" /></p>"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>CH</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>&#8211;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mo>&#8801;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Ph</mi><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mo>&#8801;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<p><img src=\"assets\\ot3_0060_b70d3df5598d.png\" style=\"width: 156px; height: 70px;\" /></p>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<p><img src=\"assets\\ot4_0060_c95585ef992d.png\" style=\"width: 129px; height: 70px;\" /></p>",
      "is_correct": true
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "D"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>Phenyl magnesium bromide is called Grignard reagent. One mole of this&nbsp;react with carbonyl compound to give alcohols. It react with aldehyde to form secondary alcohol while with ketones gives tertiary alcohols. The given compound is a tertiary alcohol so, reactant should be a ketone.</p><p><img src=\"assets\\st0060_e69182ebcd2b.png\" style=\"width: 326px; height: 100px;\" /></p></blockquote>"
  }
}